Hedging Transactions and Derivative Financial Instruments
Foreign Currency Forward Contracts Designated as Accounting Hedges
The Company enters into foreign currency forward contracts to hedge its exposure to foreign currency exchange rate risk related to future forecasted transactions denominated in currencies other than the U.S. Dollar. These contracts generally mature within 
24
 months and are designated as accounting hedges. As of September¬†27, 2025 and December¬†28, 2024, the notional value of the Company‚Äôs outstanding foreign currency forward contracts designated as cash flow hedges was $
2.3
 billion and $
2.2
