Foreign Currency Forward Contracts Not Designated as Accounting Hedges
The Company also enters into foreign currency forward contracts to reduce the short-term effects of foreign currency fluctuations on certain receivables or payables denominated in currencies other than the U.S. Dollar. These forward contracts generally mature within 
3
 months and are not designated as accounting hedges. As of September¬†27, 2025 and December¬†28, 2024, the notional value of these outstanding contracts was $
797
 million and $
